# Security review finding (fresh pre-deployment audit): with no
# .dockerignore, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile's builder stage sent the
# entire build context - including any local .env.local, .env, etc. -
# into the image, and scripts/copy-standalone-assets.mjs's own
# postbuild step (needed for the non-Docker `npm run build && npm run
# start` path, see its own header comment) then copied whichever of
# those existed straight into `.next/standalone/`, which the runner
# stage copies to `/app`. Confirmed directly: building with a real
# .env.local present left SESSION_SECRET, ACCOUNT_ENCRYPTION_KEY, and
# LICENSE_ADMIN_API_KEY sitting in `.next/standalone/.env.local` inside
# the built image. Real process env still wins over the baked file at
# runtime (verified), so this was disclosure via image layers, not an
# override risk - but a var the deployment itself doesn't set would
# silently come from whatever a dev machine's .env.local happened to
# contain.
#
# Same blanket pattern as .gitignore's own env-file exclusion, for the
# same reason: narrower forms (.env*.local + .env) would silently miss
# a stray .env.production or similar.
.env*
!.env.example

# Never needed in the build context - reinstalled fresh via
# `npm ci` in the deps stage, and re-derived by `next build` respectively.
node_modules
.next

# Git metadata and this session's own dev/CI cruft - no reason for any
# of it to reach the build context or the image.
.git
.github
*.md
!README.md

# Local dev database (SaaS-B1a, lib/db.ts - DB_FILE) - never relevant
# inside the image, which gets its own path via the Coolify volume mount.
/data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
